        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — INI parser implemented in MoonBit, `moon test` green (49/49)\n\n### What I built\nA real line-scanner + value parser in the root `ini` package (module `tonyfettes/ini`), split by responsibility:\n\n| File | Job |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ini.mbt` (91) | `parse` driver: line loop + `Builder` that routes entries to `global`/section maps (re-open section, duplicate key ⇒ last wins) |\n| `ini_scan.mbt` (186) | char classes, `split_lines` (LF/CRLF, no phantom last line), separator & inline-comment search |\n| `ini_section.mbt` (50) | `[name]` scanning: trim, strip one wrapping quote pair, reject empty/nested/trailing-text |\n| `ini_entry.mbt` (101) | first `=`/`:` split, key validation (non-empty, no control chars), backslash continuation with odd/even trailing-run rule |\n| `ini_value.mbt` (147) | quoted `\"…\"`/`'…'` values, unquoted values, inline comments, per-carrier escape decoding |\n| `ini_print.mbt` (96) | `print`: always double-quoted values with `\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t` escapes, sorted, names quoted only when needed |\n| `ini_error.mbt` (15) | `pub suberror IniError { MalformedInput(String) }` with `line N: …` messages |\n\nAll text handling uses `Array[Char]` (code points), so non-BMP values (`😀`) can't be sliced.\n\n### Tests\n* `ini_pub_test.mbt` — 12 cases: **all pass**, including both QuickCheck properties (round-trip and no-panic).\n* `ini_dialect_test.mbt` (new, 527 lines) — 35 cases derived from `specs/ini.md`: escape table (all 3 carriers), the N-backslash continuation table, separator precedence, section-name shapes, reopen/last-wins, comments, CRLF, real-world git-config/systemd/php.ini samples, every malformed form the spec requires rejecting, plus print round-trips.\n* `ini_stress_test.mbt` (new) — the two properties at 1000 iterations each.\n\n### Commands actually run\n`moon fmt` (clean), `moon info` (regenerated `pkg.generated.mbti`: `pub fn parse(StringView) -> Doc raise`, `pub fn print(Doc) -> String`), `moon check` (0 errors), `moon test` (**49 passed, 0 failed**).\n\nRemaining diagnostics are only two pre-existing ones in files I must not/should not change: `test_unqualified_package` in `ini_pub_test.mbt` and `unused_package` for `moonbitlang/core/test` in `moon.pkg`. No warning points at my code.\n\n### Independent audits (3 subagent reviews) and what they changed\nTwo audits independently found real spec violations, both now fixed and regression-tested:\n1. A quoted value could span physical lines through a trailing backslash (`k=\"abc\\` ⏎ `def\"` parsed as `abcdef`) — the closing-quote scan is now bounded by the entry's own line, so it errors per \"must be on the same physical line\".\n2. A quote arriving on a continuation line was treated as syntax (`k=\\` ⏎ `\"b\"` gave `b`) — now value syntax (quote recognition, closing quote, inline comment) is decided only on the entry's own line, so it yields the literal `\"b\"`.\nA third audit re-verified the fix (including an exhaustive fuzz of all inputs ≤5 chars over `{a \" ' \\ space ; = ⏎}`: no panics, no data loss, `parse(print(parse(t))) == parse(t)` held on all 10 324 accepted inputs).\n\n### Judgement calls left as-is (spec-silent, documented in README)\n`k=a ; c\\` ⏎ `b=1` ⇒ `k=a` with `b=1` consumed (continuation is decided on the raw line first, as the spec prescribes); a marker must be at line end (no `k=a\\ ` continuation); `<`/`>` are ordinary punctuation in section names (`<section>` alone is still rejected for having no separator); `print` cannot represent a section name containing `[`/`]`, which the dialect forbids anyway.\n\n`README.md` documents the architecture, pipeline, escape table, continuation rules, usage examples, test layout and design decisions."
        }
