          "message": "Implemented a real INI parser and printer in MoonBit for the dialect in `specs/ini.md`.\n\n## Files\n\n| file | role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `error.mbt` | `ParseError` suberror, one variant per stage (`SectionError`, `EntryError`, `ValueError`) |\n| `scan.mbt` | char classes, trimming, `split_lines`, `Lines` cursor |\n| `value.mbt` | the two value carriers (quoted / unquoted): escapes, inline comments, continuations |\n| `parser.mbt` | line classification, section headers, entry splitting, `parse` |\n| `printer.mbt` | `print` — values in the double-quoted carrier, globals first |\n| `ini_behaviour_test.mbt` | 69 spec-derived tests (kept separate from the given public suite) |\n| `README.md`, `README.mbt.md` | architecture, rules, usage, design rationale; checked example |\n\n## Behavior covered\n\n- Lines: LF/CRLF (and lone CR), blank lines, full-line `;`/`#` comments; a trailing terminator does not fabricate an empty line, which is what makes a dangling continuation a real error.\n- Sections: trimmed names, spaces/unicode/punctuation, one wrapping quote pair stripped (`[\"a b\"]` → `a b`, `remote \"origin\"` keeps its quotes), re-opening accumulates with last-wins duplicate keys, empty/nested/missing-bracket/text-after-`]` rejected.\n- Entries: first `=` or `:` wins (`url=http://host:8080/p?a=b`), key trimmed and verbatim (`key\\nname` is a backslash+n), empty/whitespace-only/control-character keys rejected.\n- Values: quoted values preserved verbatim (comment markers included), closing quote on the same line, only blanks/comment after it; per-carrier escape tables exactly as specified; inline comments only after whitespace (`key= ; c` → `\"\"`, `key=;c` → `\";c\"`); continuation decided on the raw line by trailing-backslash run parity (odd = marker, even = literals), whitespace before the marker kept, continuation lines contributing text rather than syntax.\n- `print` satisfies `parse(print(doc)) == doc`, verified by the repo's property test plus 300 arbitrary-value round-trips of my own.\n\n## Verification actually run\n\n- `moon test`: **81/81 pass** (12 public + 69 mine), also from a cold `moon clean` build.\n- `moon check`: 0 errors; the only 2 warnings are in the protected `ini_pub_test.mbt` (`Doc` qualification) and `ini_spec.mbt` (deprecated `derive(...)`). I removed the third, pre-existing `unused_package` warning by moving `moonbitlang/core/test` into a `for \"test\"` import block in `moon.pkg` (verified by tests).\n- `moon info` regenerated `pkg.generated.mbti`; `moon fmt --check` reports no diff for any file this task owns (a blanket `moon fmt` would rewrite the protected sources, so the formatter's changes were applied file by file).\n- Fuzz/robustness: 4000 grammar-soup parses (no panics), 1000 random-string parses, 500 random-document round-trips.\n- An independent review subagent audited the worktree against the spec (copy of the tree, read-only): no blocker/high findings; its three low findings were spec ambiguities I documented explicitly (outer-quote rule for section names, marker-vs-inline-comment ordering, unspecified output for out-of-dialect `Doc`s) and its nits (dead commented test, formatting, standing warning) were fixed.\n\nProtected files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `specs/`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`) were not modified."
